team-execution.summaryPrompt:
Update the Team & Execution canonical document. Instead of a markdown summary, output the summary field as a VALID JSON object (no markdown wrapping, no code fences — just raw JSON) with this exact structure:
{
  "verdict": "One-sentence investor-facing assessment of the team and execution (evidence-based).",
  "founderProfiles": [
    {
      "name": "Full Name",
      "role": "Title (e.g. Co-Founder & CEO)",
      "archetype": "Hustler | Hacker | Hipster (pick the best-fit founder archetype based on their background)",
      "background": "One-sentence summary of their most relevant prior experience",
      "linkedinSignal": "One-line signal about their credibility (e.g. 'Serial founder with healthcare exit')"
    }
  ],
  "foundersMoat": {
    "unfairAdvantage": "What makes THIS founding team uniquely positioned to win.",
    "signal": "The strongest evidence supporting the founders' moat."
  },
  "executionTimeline": [
    {
      "date": "MMM YYYY or Quarter (e.g. Oct 2024, Q4 2025)",
      "milestone": "What was achieved or is planned",
      "status": "completed | in-progress | planned"
    }
  ],
  "executionGaps": [
    {
      "gap": "Short gap title",
      "detail": "Evidence-based explanation of the gap and why it matters",
      "severity": "critical | warning"
    }
  ],
  "keyMetrics": {
    "teamSize": "Current team size string (e.g. '<10')",
    "activeUsers": "Number string or null",
    "payingCompanies": "Number string or null",
    "arr": "ARR string or null",
    "fundingRaised": "Total funding string or null"
  }
}
Rules: Include ALL named founders/key team members in founderProfiles. Archetype mapping: Hustler = sales/BD/growth focus; Hacker = technical/engineering focus; Hipster = product/design/brand focus. Timeline should have 4-8 milestones ordered chronologically. ExecutionGaps should have 3-6 items, severity 'critical' for deal-breaker risks and 'warning' for addressable concerns. Keep all text concise and evidence-backed. Use wording Data not Canonical Package.
